hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1123","It was narrated from Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Jizya from the Magi of Hijra. (Narrated by Al-Bukhari. And there is another chain of transmission of this hadith in Muta which has an interruption.)"
"1124","Mr. Asim bin Umar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) and Hazrat Uthman bin Abi Sulaiman (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Hazrat Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him) to Uqadir, the ruler of Dumat al-Jandal. Hazrat Khalid (RA) and his companions arrested him and took him to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). You did not shed his blood and reconciled with him on Jizya. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud.)"
"1125","Hazrat Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent me to Yemen and ordered me to take one dinar or its equivalent (value) of travel cloth from every adult. (It has been narrated by all three and Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim have declared it Sahih.)"
"1126","Hazrat Aiz bin Amr Muzni (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “Islam prevails and is not defeated.” (Narrated by Darqutani)."
"1127","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not take the initiative to greet the Jews and Christians, and when you meet one of them on the way, force him to go to the narrow side of the way.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1128","It is narrated from Hazrat Miswar bin Makharma (RA) and Marwan that the Prophet (PBUH) came out in the year of Hudaybiyyah. The narrator has narrated a long hadith and it is mentioned in it: “This is the (document) on which Muhammad bin Abdullah (peace be upon him) reconciled with Suhail bin Amr that war would cease for ten years. During this period, people will live in peace and each of them will keep their hand from the other (from fighting).” (Narrated by Abu Dawud and its original is in Bukhari) And Imam Muslim narrated a part of this hadith from Hazrat Anas Radiyallahu Anhu and it says: Whoever among you comes to us, we will not return him to you, and whoever of our men comes to you today, you will return him to us. The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah! Shall we write this too? He said: \"Yes! Whoever among us went to them, Allah reprimanded him, and whoever among them came to us, Allah will certainly make a way for him to escape."
"1129","Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Whoever kills a covenant will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, although its fragrance will be smelled from a distance of forty years.” (Bukhari)"
"1130","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the tamed horses run from Hafiyyah to Thaniyyah al-Wada'a and the horses that were not tamed ran from Tanimyah to the mosque of Bani Zariq. And Hazrat Ibn Umar was among the winners of the race. (Bukhari and Muslim) and there is an addition in Bukhari that Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) stated that the distance from Hafiyyah to Thaniyyah al-Wadaa is five or six miles. And the distance from Saniya to Masjid Bani Zariq is one mile."
"1131","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arranged a horse race and kept the young horses at a longer distance. (Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud, and Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
"1132","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Competition is permissible only in three things: camel racing, shooting, or horse racing.\""
"1133","Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: \"There is no harm in a person who puts a third horse between two horses and is not afraid of his horse being left behind.\" And if he is not afraid (of being left behind by his horse) (and he is sure of going ahead of it) then it is gambling.” (Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud and its chain of transmission is weak."
"1134","On the authority of Hazrat Uqba bin Aamir, may Allah be pleased with him, I heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was standing on the pulpit and reciting this (verse): ) And promise them what you can from the strength and from the ties of the horses... (Al-Anfal 8:60) Therefore, according to your ability, prepare to keep the force and horses ready.\" Then he said: \"Listen! Strength is targetting. Listen! Strength is targetting. Listen! Force is 'targeting' (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1135","Hazrat Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “It is forbidden to eat any animal that is scratched.” (Narrated by Muslim.) And Muslim narrated the same tradition on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) with the words that he forbade... and this is added: “It is forbidden to eat any bird that hunts with its claws.”"
"1136","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaibar and allowed the meat of horses. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in the tradition of Bukhari, instead of AZIN, there is the word Rakhs, which means that you gave leave."
"1137","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abi Ufaa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We fought seven battles with the Prophet, peace be upon him, and we used to eat locusts. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1138","On the authority of Hazrat Anas (RA) regarding the story of the rabbit, he says that he (Abu Laha) slaughtered it and offered its thigh to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he accepted it. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1139","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade the killing of four animals: the ant, the bee, the wasp, and the latura. (It was narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud. And Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
"1140","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abi Ammar, may God have mercy on him, that I asked Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace, whether Laggar is also a victim. He said: Yes. I asked again: (What) has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? He said: Yes. (It was narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu, and Bukhari and Ibn Hibban declared it authentic.)"
"1141","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that he was asked about Khar Pusht. In response, he recited this commandment of Allah: ﴾Qul-la-ajiddu fi-ma-uhi-ya-li-ya-muharramma...﴾Al-Ayah (Al-Anaam 6:145) (O Messenger! Say that I do not find anything forbidden in what has been revealed to me...) There was an elder sitting next to him. He was saying that this (Kharpasht) was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: “This is one of the evil (animals).” (Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud and its chain of transmission is weak."
"1142","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the consumption of dirt-eating animals and their milk. (Except for Nasai, it has been narrated by all four. And Tirmidhi has described it as Hasan.)"
"1143","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Qatadah (RA) regarding the story of the wild donkey that the Prophet (PBUH) ate its meat. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1144","It was narrated from Hazrat Asmaa bint Abi Bakr (RA) that we slaughtered a horse during the reign of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and ate it. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1145","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Zab (Sanda) was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1146","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman Quraishi that a physician asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the use of a frog as medicine, and he forbade killing it. (It was narrated by Ahmad and Al-Hakim called it Sahih.)"
"1147","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever keeps a dog (as a hobby or for any other reason) other than protecting livestock, hunting or farming, then his reward will be reduced by one carat every day.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1148","On the authority of Hadhrat Udi bin Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \"When you leave your dog (for hunting), recite Bismillah over it.\" And if he finds the victim dead and the dog has not yet eaten anything of it, he may eat it. And if you find another dog with your dog and find it dead, then do not eat it, because you do not know which of them killed it. And if you miss your arrow, recite Bismillah over it. Then if the prey remains out of your sight for a day and there is no wound in it other than your arrow, then if you wish, eat it. And if you find the victim drowned in water, do not eat it.” (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
"1149","It was narrated from Hadhrat Adi, may Allah be pleased with him, that I asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting a diseased animal, and he said: \"If you hit it from the tip, then eat it, and if you hit it from the broad side, and the animal dies, then it is an animal that has died of injury, so do not eat it.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1150","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Thaalba, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When you shoot a game with your arrow and it disappears from your sight, then you find it later, then eat it until it smells bad.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1151","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that some people asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that people bring meat to us about which we do not know whether they have mentioned the name of Allah on it or not. He said: \"You mention the name of Allah on it and eat it.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"1152","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah Bin Mughfil Muzni (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade throwing pebbles and said: \"It (pebbles) cannot hunt or injure the enemy, but it will break someone's tooth or tear someone's eye.\" (Bukhari and Muslim, and these words are Muslim's)."
"1153","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not target and kill any living thing.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1154","It was narrated from Hazrat Ka'b bin Malik (RA) that a woman slaughtered a goat with a stone (sharp edge of a stone). (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1155","Hazrat Rafi bin Khadij (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “Anything (of an animal) that sheds blood and the name of Allah has been mentioned on it, then eat that animal. Except for teeth and nails, because teeth are bones and nails are the knives of the Abyssinians.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1156","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) forbade killing an animal by tying it. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1157","On the authority of Hazrat Shaddad bin Aws, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah the Exalted has made it obligatory to be kind to everything.\" And every one of you should sharpen his knife and rest his slaughtered.\" (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1158","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When the mother slaughters the fetus, the fetus is slaughtered by itself.\""
"1159","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “His name alone is sufficient for a Muslim.” So, if he forgets to mention the name of Allah at the time of slaughter, then he should recite Bismillah and eat. Narrated this tradition with authentic authority from Imam Abu Dawud, and there is also a witness of it in the Messengers of Imam Abu Dawud. The words of this tradition are: \"The slaughter of a Muslim is lawful, whether the name of Allah is mentioned on it or not.\""
"1160","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two rams with horns and horns, and recite Bismillah and say Takbeer and place his blessed feet on their sides. And there is a tradition that you slaughtered them both with your blessed hand. (Bukhari and Muslim) and there is a tradition that he was very fat. And in the Sahih of Abu Awana, instead of Saminin, there is saminin, which means they were precious. And there is a hadith of Muslim that he used to say in the name of Allah and Allah is the greatest. And in the hadeeth of Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, it is narrated in Muslim that he ordered a horned ram that walks in black (its legs are black), sits in black (its belly and chest are black) and sees in black (its eyes are also black) so that you may sacrifice it. So he said: ('Aisha!) Sharpen the knife.' Then he took hold of the knife and killed the ram. Then, while slaughtering him, he said: [In the name of Allah! Accept from Muhammad and the family of Muhammad] “In the name of Allah (I slaughter) O Allah! Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, \"Accept it on behalf of the family of Muhammad and the nation of Muhammad.\" Then he sacrificed it."
"1161","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever has the power to sacrifice and does not sacrifice, then he should not come near our place of Eid.\""
"1162","Hazrat Jundab bin Sufyan (RA) narrated that I was present in the assembly of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) on Eid-ul-Adha. So when you had led the people to pray, you saw that a goat had been slaughtered. He said: \"Whoever slaughtered before the prayer should slaughter another goat in its place, and whoever did not slaughter it should slaughter it after reciting Bismillah.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1163","On the authority of Hazrat Bara bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood among us and said: \"There are four types of defects that should not be found in sacrificial animals: the lameness of the goats is obvious, the sick animal whose disease is obvious, the lame animal whose lameness is prominent and visible, and the very old animal without pulp in its bones.\" given.)"
"1164","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Slaughter only two teeth (in the sacrifice), but if you are faced with difficulty and difficulty, then slaughter a leg of the sheep's skin.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1165","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that we look carefully at the eyes and ears of the sacrificial animal. And we should not slaughter an animal whose ear is cut in front or behind, or whose ear is pierced, or whose ear is cut lengthwise. ,, (It was narrated by Ahmad and the four. Tirmidhi, Ibn Hibban and Hakim declared it to be Sahih.)"
"1166","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed me to look after his sacrificial camels and ordered me to distribute their meat, skins and dung among the poor and not to give any of it as a butcher's wages. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1167","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that we sacrificed a camel and a cow with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) on behalf of seven men on the occasion of the Peace of Hudaybiyah. (Muslim)"
"1168","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed one ram each on behalf of Hazrat Hasan and Hazrat Hussain (RA). (It was narrated by Abu Dawud. And Ibn Khuzimah, Ibn Jarood and Abdul Haq called it Sahih, but Abu Hatim preferred it to be sent by him, and Ibn Hibban narrated a similar tradition regarding Hazrat Anas, may God be pleased with him.)"
"1169","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his Companions to slaughter two identical goats from the boy and one goat from the girl. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi and declared it to be Sahih, Ahmad and the four narrated a similar tradition from Umm Kurz Kaabiyyah.)"
"1170","It is narrated from Hazrat Samurah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Every child is a pledge (mortgage) for his aqiqah.\" On the seventh day (of birth) he should be aqeeqah, his head should be shaved and his name should be given."
"1171","Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (SAW) that he heard Hazrat Umar (RA) taking the oath of his father in a caravan, so the Messenger of Allah (SAW) called him and said: “Listen! Allah has forbidden you from swearing by your fathers and forefathers, so if you want to swear, then swear by Allah, otherwise remain silent.'' Swear by Allah only when you are truthful."
"1172","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Your oath will be on that which your partner believes you to be true to.\" And in one tradition, it is said: \"An oath depends on the intention of the one who takes the oath.\" (These two hadiths were narrated by Muslim)."
"1173","It was narrated from Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When you take an oath for a deed, then consider another deed to be better than it, then make expiation for the oath and do what is better.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) Do it, then do what is better after that.” (This narration is authentic.)"
"1174","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever swears to do something and at the same time says, In shaa Allah, there is no crime of breaking his oath.\""
"1175","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the swearing words of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, were: \"No! By Him Who turns hearts.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1176","It is narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr that a villager came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! What are the major sins? (Then the narrator narrated the whole hadith.) In this hadith it is: \"False swearing (is also a great sin.\") And it also has this: I asked: What is a false oath? He said: \"A false oath is one by which a Muslim's property is stolen, even though he (the swearer) is a complete liar.\" (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1177","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that she said in the interpretation of Allah's saying: \"Allah will not charge you with your false oaths\" (Al-Baqarah 2:225). Yes, by God! (Narrated by al-Bukhari and narrated by Abu Dawood with authority.)"
"1178","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, there are ninety-nine names of Allah, whoever memorizes them, he will enter Paradise.\""
"1179","On the authority of Hazrat Osama bin Zayd, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever is treated with goodness and good behavior, and he says to the one who does good and benevolent: [Jazak Allahu Khair] May Allah reward you with good. So he paid the right to praise him.”"
"1180","Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) has narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he forbade taking vows and said: “Vows do not lead to good or good. Only the wealth of a miser is taken out through it.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1181","On the authority of Hazrat Uqba bin Aamir, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \"The expiation of a vow is an expiation of an oath.\" (Muslim) Tirmidhi has added this addition to it: \"When he does not determine it.\" And whoever took the vow of sin, then his expiation is also an expiation. And whoever takes a vow that he does not have the power to do, then his expiation is only an expiation of an oath. Not true."
"1182","It was narrated from Hazrat Uqba bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) that my sister took a vow to walk barefoot to the House of Allah and he ordered me to inquire about it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I asked him, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Walk on foot and ride.” No need. Order him to put on a cloak and ride and fast for three days."
"1183","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that Hazrat Sa'd bin Ubadah (RA) asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about this vow, which was the duty of the young man's mother and she died before fulfilling it. He said: \"Then complete it on his behalf.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1184","It was narrated from Hazrat Thabit bin Dahhak (may God be pleased with him) that during the blessed reign of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) a man took a vow to slaughter a camel at the place of \"Bawana\". He asked: \"Didn't they have a festival there?\" The man said: No. Then he said: \"Fulfill your vow.\" One should not fulfill a vow which involves disobedience to Allah or a cut of mercy which is not within the power of the son of Adam."
"1185","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir that a person said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: O Messenger of Allah! I had taken a vow that if Allah Ta'ala conquers Makkah in your hands, I will pray in Bait al-Maqdis. He said: \"Read here.\" He asked again, so he said: \"Read here.\" He asked again, and he said: \"Your will.\""
"1186","Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One should not travel to any place except three mosques for the purpose of reward: Masjid al-Haram, Masjid al-Aqsa, and my mosque (Masjid al-Nabawi.”) (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Bukhari)."
"1187","It was narrated from Hazrat Umar (RA) that I said: O Messenger of Allah! I had taken a vow during the Jahiliyyah era that I would perform I'tikaf for one night in Masjid Haram. He said: \"Fulfill your vow.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) And there is this addition in a tradition of Bukhari: Then he performed I'tikaf for one night."
"1188","Narrated by Hazrat Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There are three types of judges: two are from hell and one is from heaven: the person who recognizes the truth and decides according to it is the one from heaven.\" And the person who recognized the truth, but did not judge with the truth, but was unjust in deciding, then he is in Hell, and the person who did not recognize the truth, but judged people out of ignorance and ignorance, then he is also in Hell."
"1189","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The person who was appointed to judge was slaughtered without a knife.\""
"1190","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, you people will certainly covet and desire the government, and it will certainly be a source of regret on the Day of Resurrection.\" So the one who breastfeeds is good and the one who is weaned is bad.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1191","It was narrated from Hazrat Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"When a ruler deliberates carefully while making a decision, then succeeds in making a correct decision, he gets a double reward, and when he deliberates in making a decision but makes a mistake in making a decision, he will receive a reward.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1192","Hazrat Abu Bakra (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say: “No one should decide between two people in a state of anger.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1193","On the authority of Hazrat Ali, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When two men come to you for a decision, do not decide in favor of one of them until you hear what the other has to say.\" From this you will know how you have to make a decision. Hazrat Ali said: Since this teaching, I make decisions in the same way. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Tirmidhi called it Hasan, and Ibn Madini called it strong, and Ibn Hibban called it Sahih. And the Hadith of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, is a witness to it.)"
"1194","It is narrated from Umm Salama (RA) that she said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Indeed, you people bring your disputes to me, and sometimes one of you presents his arguments to the opposing side in a very polite manner, so I decide in his favor according to what I hear from him.\" Therefore, if I give something from his brother's right, I am giving him a piece of fire.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1195","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"How can a nation be pure in which the rights of the weak cannot be taken from the strong?\""
"1196","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “On the Day of Judgment, a just judge will be called to account. He will realize the severity of his account and wish that he had not made a single decision between two people in his lifetime.” (Narrated by Ibn Hibban and narrated by Bayhaqi.)"
"1197","Hazrat Abu Bakra (RA) has narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “A nation will never prosper which makes a woman its ruler and ruler.” (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"1198","Hazrat Abu Maryam Azdi (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “Whoever Allah Almighty has made the ruler and responsible for any task of the Muslims and he continues to refrain from fulfilling their needs and wants (remains in hijab), then Allah Ta’ala will also veil him from fulfilling his needs.” (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi)."
"1199","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the bribe-giver and the bribe-taker. (It has been narrated by Ahmad and the four. And Tirmidhi has declared it hasan and Ibn Hibban has called it Sahih. The hadith of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, is a witness of this in the case of the four, except for Nasa'i.)"
"1200","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Zubair that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the parties should sit in front of the ruler. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Hakim declared it Sahih.)"
"1201","On the authority of Hazrat Zaid bin Khalid Jahni, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Shall I not inform you about the best witness?\" (The best witness) is the one who comes to testify without being asked to testify.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1202","On the authority of Hazrat Imran bin Hussain, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The best of you are the people of my time, then those after them, then those after them, then there will be people who will testify and they will not be asked to testify.\" They will be traitors, they will not be faithful. They will take vows but not fulfill them, and obesity will be prominent among them.” (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1203","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The testimony of a traitorous man or woman is not permissible, and the testimony of a slanderous person against his (Muslim) brother is not permissible, and the testimony of a servant (servant) is not permissible in favor of his family.\" (Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud)."
"1204","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"The testimony of a nomad is not acceptable against a citizen.\" (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah)."
"1205","On the authority of Hazrat Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he gave a sermon and said that during the time of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, people were prosecuted through revelation. Now the revelation is closed, now we will accuse you based on your deeds that will be revealed to us. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1206","Hazrat Abu Bakra (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he considered false testimony as one of the major sins. (This is in a long hadith of Bukhari and Muslim.)"
"1207","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: \"Are you looking at the sun?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Give this kind of testimony, otherwise let it remain.\""
"1208","It was narrated from Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) decided on the basis of an oath and a witness. (It was narrated by Muslim, Abu Dawud and Nasa’i. And Nasa’i said that its chain of transmission is excellent.)"
"1209","A similar tradition has been narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him). (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
"1210","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If people are given rights simply by claiming them, people will start claiming other people's blood and their property, but (the principle is) an oath is required on the defendant.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1211","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an oath in front of some people and they immediately got ready to take the oath. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1212","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Umamah al-Harithi, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever violates the right of a Muslim man through his oath, Allah will make Hellfire obligatory for him, and Jannah will be forbidden for him.\" A person said: O Messenger of Allah! Although something despised and insignificant? He said: \"Even if there is a branch of the yellow.\" (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1213","It is narrated from Hazrat Ash'ath bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever steals the property of a Muslim by taking an oath, while he is a liar in his oath, he will appear before Allah in such a state that Allah will be very angry with him.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1214","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Musa that two men quarreled about an animal. None of them had any arguments, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided to divide the animal between them. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Nasa'i, these words are from Nasa'i. And Imam Nasa'i said that its chain of transmission is Jaid.)"
"1215","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever swears falsely on this pulpit of mine, has made his abode in Hell.\""
"1216","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three people to whom Allah will speak on the Day of Judgment, neither will He look at them (mercy) nor cleanse them from their sins, but there will be a painful punishment for them: (First) The person who stays near water left in the desert and stops a traveler from it. And (second) the man who trades something with another after Asr and swears by Allah that he has bought this thing for so much and the buyer accepts it as true, although the reality is the opposite. And (third) the person who pledged allegiance to a king for worldly purposes only, if the king gives him something, then he is loyal, and if he does not give him anything, then he is not loyal.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1217","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Jabir that two men quarreled about a camel. Each of them claimed that it was born in me and both presented their own arguments. Therefore, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his decision in favor of the person in whose hands it was."
"1218","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) swore an oath to the claimant. (Both of these hadiths have been narrated by Darqutni, and both of them are weak in their chain of transmission.)"
"1219","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she says that one day the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me. Anwar's letters were shining on you. He said: \"Don't you know that Majaz Madalji has just seen Zayd bin Haritha and Usamah bin Zayd and said that these feet are a part of each other.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1220","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a Muslim man, Allah will save each of his limbs from the fire of Hell for each limb.” And it is in the hadith narrated by Hazrat Ka'b bin Murrah (RA) in Abu Dawud: \"A Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman will be the cause of her release from Hell.\""
"1221","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Dharr that I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which is the best deed. He said: \"Believing in Allah and doing Jihad in His way.\" I said: Which slave is better to free? He said: \"The one who is more expensive in price and more refined and beloved in the eyes of the owners.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1222","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees his share of a common slave, then he has enough wealth to pay the value of the slave, then his value will be determined justly, then he will pay his share (the price) to his sharers, and this slave will be freed on his behalf.” And if he does not have excess wealth, then whatever portion he frees will be freed.” (Bukhari and Muslim) And both (Bukhari and Muslim) have quoted these words from Hazrat Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him): “Otherwise, a price will be imposed on him and he will be made to work without laboring on him to free him.”"
"1223","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"No son can repay his father except if the father is a slave, then he should buy him and set him free.\" (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1224","On the authority of Hazrat Samura bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever becomes the owner of a relative of a mahram, then he (the relative) is free.”"
"1225","It is narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain that a man freed six of his slaves at the time of his death. He had no other property except these slaves. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them (the slaves) and divided them into three parts, then drew lots among them. So he freed two and allowed four to remain slaves and also spoke harsh words in favor of the freedman. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1226","It was narrated from Hazrat Safina (RA) that I was a slave of Hazrat Umm Salama (RA). He said: I set you free and make a condition that you will serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as long as you live. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud, Nasa’i and Hakim)."
"1227","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"And the right belongs to him who frees.\" (Bukhari and Muslim. This is a fragment of a long hadith.)"
"1228","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There is also a relationship like the relationship of descent, which cannot be sold or given away.\""
"1229","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that an Ansari made one of his slaves a slave and he had no other property except him. This matter reached the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: \"Who will buy this slave from me?\" So Hazrat Nu'aym bin Abdullah (RA) bought him for eight hundred dirhams. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in a tradition of Bukhari: So he (Ansari) became needy. And there is a tradition of Nasa'i that he (Ansari) had a debt, so he sold it for eight hundred dirhams and gave him this price and said: \"Pay your debt.\""
"1230","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father and he from his grandfather. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"A student is a slave as long as there is even one dirham left for him from his correspondence.\""
"1231","On the authority of Hazrat Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When a woman among you has a school and has enough wealth to pay for it, then she (the woman) should cover herself with it.\""
"1232","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “To the extent that the school has become free, the free man’s diet will be paid, and to the extent that it is a slave, the slave’s diet will be paid.” (Narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dada and Nasa’i)."
"1233","It was narrated from Hazrat Amr bin Harith, the brother of Umm al-Momineen Hazrat Juwayriyya (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) did not leave a single dirham, nor a dinar, nor a slave, nor a slave girl, nor anything else except a white mule, weapons of war, and a small amount of land which he had given as charity at the time of his death. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1234","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A slave girl who gives birth to her master's child is free after the death of the master.\""
"1235","On the authority of Hazrat Sahl bin Hunaif, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever helps a mujahid in the cause of Allah, or helps a debtor in need, or helps him pay the fees of a school, Allah will give him shade on a day when there will be no shade except his shade.”"
"1236","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A Muslim has six rights over another Muslim: When you meet him, greet him; When he calls you, fulfill his request; When he asks you for good wishes, wish him well.\" Allah say, 'When he falls ill, visit him and when he dies, follow his funeral' (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1237","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Look at those who are inferior to you and do not look at those who are superior to you, because in this way it is more appropriate that you will not despise any of the blessings of God.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1238","It was narrated from Hazrat Nawas bin Samaan (RA) that I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about virtue and sin, and he said: \"Virtue is the name of good conduct and sin is that which strikes your heart and you find it distasteful that people should become aware of it.\" (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1239","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When there are three of you, two men should not whisper without the third, until you mingle with the people, because this thing makes him sad and distressed.\" (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
"1240","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"No man should lift someone from his place and sit in that place himself, but (if there is a lack of space, he should tell the people of the assembly to) expand and expand.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1241","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When one of you eats, he should not clean his hand (with a handkerchief, etc.) before licking or wiping it.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1242","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Greet the small and the big, the one who is walking and the one who is sitting on the road, and those who are a little more numerous.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) and in a tradition of Muslim, there is:"
"1243","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"When a group passes by someone, it is enough for one person to greet them, and it is enough for one person to respond.\" (Narrated by Ahmad and Bayhaqi)."
"1244","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not take the initiative to greet the Jews and Christians, and when you meet them on the way, force them to the narrow path.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1245","Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “When one of you sneezes, he should say Al-Hamdu-Lillah (All praise is due to Allah) and his brother should say Yarhamuk-Allah (May Allah have mercy on you). When he says Yarhamuk Allah, then the person who sneezes should say in response: Yahdikum Allah wa yuslihu baalkum (May Allah guide you and correct your situation) (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"1246","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"None of you should drink water while standing.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1247","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When one of you puts on a shoe, put it on the right foot first, and when you take it off, take it off with the left foot first.\" That is, the right foot should be the first to put on the shoe and the last to take it off."
"1248","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “None of you should walk around wearing one shoe, either wear both together or take them off.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1249","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah will not look with mercy on a person who hangs his garment down (ankles, etc.) out of arrogance.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1250","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whenever one of you eats, he should eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, he should drink with his right hand, because Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left.\" (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1251","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father and he from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Eat, drink, wear clothes and give charity, but without extravagance and arrogance.”"
"1252","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever wishes that his sustenance should be extended and his life extended, he should offer Salah al-Rahmi.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"1253","On the authority of Hazrat Jubayr bin Mut'am, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who cuts off the womb will not enter Paradise.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1254","It was narrated from Hazrat Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah has made it forbidden for you to disobey mothers and mistreat them, to bury girls alive, to not pay your rights, and to spread your hands in front of others."
"1255","Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: “The pleasure of Allah is in the approval of the parents, and the displeasure of Allah is in the displeasure of the parents.”"
"1256","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"By the Most Holy One in Whose Hand is my soul! A person cannot be a believer until he does not like for his neighbor or his brother what he likes for himself.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1257","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, I asked the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Which sin is the greatest? He said: \"That you associate anyone with Allah, even though He is your Creator.\" I said: Then which one? He said: \"That you should kill your children for fear that they will eat together with you.\" I then asked which one? He said: \"Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1258","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Abusing one's parents is one of the major sins.\" It was said: Does a person abuse his parents? He said: \"Yes!\" If he abuses someone's father, then he abuses his father, and if he abuses his mother, then he abuses his mother.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1259","On the authority of Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to have intercourse with his brother for more than three nights.\" When the two face each other, it turns its mouth this way and he turns this way. The better of the two is the one who initiates peace.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1260","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Every good thing is charity.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"1261","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Dharr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not despise any good deed, even if it is meeting your brother with a smile on your face.\""
"1262","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Dharr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When you cook broth, add a little more water to it and take care of your neighbor.\" (These two hadiths were narrated by Muslim.)"
"1263","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever removes the hardships and hardships of a Muslim from the hardships of this world, Allah will remove one of the hardships from him from the hardships of the Day of Resurrection.\" And whoever makes it easy for someone who is in need, Allah will make it easy for him in this world and in the hereafter. And whoever hides the fault of a Muslim, Allah will cover him in this world and in the hereafter. And Allah, the Exalted, helps a servant as long as he helps his brother.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1264","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever guides the path of goodness, he will receive the same reward as the one who practices good deeds.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1265","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever asks you for refuge in the name of Allah, give him refuge, and whoever asks you in the name of Allah, grant him, and whoever treats you kindly and benevolently, reward him for kindness.\" If you do not have the power to retaliate, then pray for him.” (Narrated by Bayhaqi)."
"1266","It was narrated from Hazrat Numan bin Basheer (RA) that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and Hazrat Numan raised his two fingers to his ears saying: \"Surely the lawful is also clear\" and undoubtedly the forbidden is also clear. And in between these two are suspicious things that most people don't know about. Therefore, whoever is saved from doubts, he has saved his religion and his honor and reputation. And he who fell into doubt was caught in the Haram. Like a shepherd grazing (cattle) around a pasture, it is possible that an animal may enter it. Beware! Of course, every king has a pasture. Beware! Verily, the pastures of Allah are the forbidden things. Beware! Indeed, there is a piece of flesh in the body, when it is right, the whole body is right, and when it is corrupted, the whole body is corrupted. Beware! That piece is the heart.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1267","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \"The servant of a dinar, a dirham, and a cloak has perished.\""
"1268","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, took hold of my shoulders and said: \"(O Ibn Umar!) Live in this world like a stranger or a traveler on the road.\" And Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: When it is evening, do not wait for the morning, and when it is morning, do not wait for the evening, and prepare for your illness when you are healthy and for death in life. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1269","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever imitates another nation, he is one of them.\""
"1270","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas that one day I was (standing) behind the Prophet. He said: \"O boy! So guard Allah's commandments, Allah will guard you. So if you guard Allah's commandments, you will find it in front of you. And when you ask for something, ask (only) Allah, and when you ask for help, then (only) ask Allah for help."
"1271","It is narrated from Hazrat Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me such a deed that when I do it, Allah will make me his beloved and people will also love me. He said: \"Be free from the world and Allah will make you beloved.\" And be independent of what people have, and people will love you.”"
"1272","It was narrated from Hazrat Saad bin Abi Waqqas (RA) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “Allah loves a servant who is pious, selfless and anonymous (hidden).” (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1273","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A person's giving up useless things is the proof of his good Islam.\""
"1274","On the authority of Hazrat Muqadam bin Maadikarb, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The son of Adam did not fill a vessel worse than his stomach.”"
"1275","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Every son of Adam is a sinner, and the best sinners are those who repent most.\""
"1276","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Silence is wisdom, but there are few who follow it.\""
"1277","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Save yourself from envy,\" because envy eats up good deeds like fire (dry) eats wood."
"1278","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who knocks someone down is not brave.\" Brave is he who controls himself in anger.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1279","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Oppression will be the cause of much darkness on the Day of Resurrection.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1280","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Beware of oppression, for oppression will be in the form of darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and also beware of miserliness, for it has killed people before you.\" (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1281","It is narrated from Hazrat Mahmud bin Labaid, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The most I fear about you is your shirk asghar\" (hypocrisy)."
"1282","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There are three signs of a hypocrite: When he speaks, he lies.\" And when he promises, he breaks his promise. And when a trust is placed with him, he should betray it.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) And both of them have it in the tradition of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them: \"When they fight, abuse them.\""
"1283","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Masoud that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Abusing a Muslim is Fiqh and fighting him is Kufr.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1284","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Beware of suspicion, because suspicion is the greatest lie.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1285","On the authority of Hazrat Muaqal bin Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever Allah Almighty makes the ruler of the people and he dies in such a state that he has not fulfilled the rights of his subjects, then Allah Almighty forbids Paradise for him.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1286","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God! Whoever makes my ummah the head of a task and makes them suffer hardship, then be strict with him.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1287","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whenever one of you fights, he should avoid hitting on the face.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1288","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace: Give me some advice. He said: \"Don't be angry.\" He repeated the same question several times and each time he said: \"Don't be angry.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1289","It is narrated from Hazrat Khula Ansariyyah, she says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Some people interfere unjustly in the wealth of Allah.\" For such people is the fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1290","Hazrat Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) has narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the news that he narrates from Allah Almighty that Allah Almighty said: “O my servants! Verily, I have forbidden oppression upon myself and have declared it forbidden among you, so do not oppress one another.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1291","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do you know what is called backsliding?\" The Companions said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Backbiting is when you mention your brother in a way that he dislikes.\" Someone said: What I say, if it is found in my brother? He said: \"What you say, if it is found in it, then you have backbited it, and if it is not in it, then you have slandered it.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1292","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not be jealous of one another, do not raise prices (in order to deceive) do not hold grudges against one another, do not be partial to one another, and do not bargain at the expense of one another.\" Servants of Allah! Be brothers to each other. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. He oppresses him and does not leave him helpless and does not despise him.\" And he pointed to his chest three times and said: \"Taqwa is here. Evil is enough for a man to despise his Muslim brother. The blood, property and honor of every Muslim is forbidden to another Muslim.” (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1293","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Qutba bin Malik, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say these words of supplication: [Allahhum! Janibni Munkarat al-Akhlaaq' and al-A'mal' and al-Ahwa' and al-Adwaa'] \"God! Save me from bad manners, bad deeds, bad desires and bad diseases.”"
"1294","Narrated by Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not quarrel with your Muslim brother, nor joke with him, and do not make a promise to him that you may later break.\""
"1295","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There are two traits that cannot be gathered in a believer: miserliness and bad manners.\""
"1296","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Two men who abuse each other, no matter what they say, the burden of sin is (only) on the one who initiates it until the oppressed abuses it.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1297","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Sarmah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever harms a Muslim, Allah will harm him, and whoever causes hardship to a Muslim, Allah will cause him hardship and distress.”"
"1298","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, Allah hates the obscene and foul-mouthed.\""
"1299","And in Tirmidhi, there is a tradition of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him: “A believer is not one who slanders a lot, curses a lot, is obscene, and does not speak badly.”"
"1300","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Do not abuse the dead, for they have reached what they sent forth.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1301","On the authority of Hazrat Hudhayfah, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A gluttonous person will not enter Paradise.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1302","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will restrain His punishment from him.\""
"1303","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “A cheater, a miser, and a bad-tempered person will not enter Paradise.”"
"1304","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever secretly tries to listen to the speech of a people while they dislike him, lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection.\" (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1305","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There is good news for that person whose fault prevents him from (finding) the faults of other people.\""
"1306","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever thinks himself great and arrogant in his behavior will meet Allah in such a state that He will be angry with him.\""
"1307","On the authority of Hazrat Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Haste and haste are evil acts.\""
"1308","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: “Bad behavior is bad.” (Narrated by Ahmad and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
"1309","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Certainly those who curse will be intercessors on the Day of Judgment, not witnesses.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1310","On the authority of Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever makes his brother ashamed of a sin, he himself will die doing the same thing.\""
"1311","Hazrat Bahz bin Hakeem narrated from his father and he narrated from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Death to the person who tells lies and makes people laugh.\" There is destruction upon him, then there is destruction upon him."
"1312","On the authority of Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The expiation for the one whom you have backstabbed is to seek forgiveness (from Allah) for him.”"
"1313","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"The most hateful of the servants of Allah is the one who is the most quarrelsome.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1314","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Establish the truth because the truth leads to goodness, and goodness leads to Paradise.\" And a person always speaks the truth and seeks the truth until it is written as siddiqiq with Allah. And avoid lies because lies lead to sin and sin leads to hell fire. And a man always lies and seeks lies until he is written as a liar before Allah.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1315","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Beware of suspicion.\" Suspicion is the biggest lie.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1316","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Avoid sitting on the roads.\" The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah! We do not live without sitting in the streets because we sit there and talk. He said: \"If you want, then pay the right of way.\" He said: What is his right? He said: \"Keeping the eyes down, refraining from causing trouble, answering greetings, enjoining good and forbidding evil.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1317","It is narrated from Hazrat Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah, the Exalted, bestows upon him whom He intends good, the understanding of religion.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1318","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There is nothing heavier in the scales than good conduct.\""
"1319","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Modesty is a part of faith.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1320","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"From what the people have found in the words of the first (past) Prophethood, this is also that when you become indecent, do whatever you want.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1321","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A strong believer is more beloved to Allah than a weak and weak believer.\" And there is goodness in every believer. Be greedy for what is beneficial to you. Don't just ask Allah for help and don't sit down feeling helpless. And if any trouble befalls you, do not say that if I had done this work in this way, I would have received these and these benefits. Rather, by saying in this way that Allah, the Exalted, decreed and showed what He willed. Because the word ``If'' opens the door to Satan's action."
"1322","It is narrated from Hazrat Ayyad bin Hammar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Surely, Allah Almighty has revealed to me that you should be humble and obedient.\" So that no one abuses another, and no one is proud of another.\" (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1323","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Darda, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever protects his brother's honor in his absence, Allah will keep the fire of hell away from his face on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"1324","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Charity and charity do not diminish any wealth.\" And Allah increases the honor of the one who forgives. And whoever humbles himself before Allah, Allah exalts him.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1325","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Salam that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People! Spread the greetings, show mercy, feed them, and pray at night when others are sleeping, and you will enter Paradise in peace.”"
"1326","Narrated by Hazrat Tamim Dari, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Deen is the name of good will.\" He said this three times. We said: O Messenger of Allah! Goodwill for whom? He said: \"For Allah, for His Book, for His Messenger, for the Imams of the Muslims and for their common people.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1327","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The thing that will most lead to entering Paradise is the fear of Allah and good character.\""
"1328","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"You cannot gain access to people through your wealth, but you can gain access to people through generosity and good manners.\""
"1329","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah said: \"A believer is the mirror of his believing brother.\" (Narrated by Abu Dawud with a good chain of transmission.)"
"1330","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The believer who keeps company with the people and is patient with their persecution is better than the believer who does not keep company with the people and is not patient with their persecution.\""
"1331","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"O Allah, just as You have made my creation (shape and form) good, so make my conduct good.\""
"1332","On the authority of Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah, the Exalted, says that I am with my servant as long as he remembers me and his lips move with my remembrance.\""
"1333","On the authority of Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The son of Adam did not do anything more than the remembrance of Allah, which would save him more from the punishment of God.\""
"1334","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whenever a people sits in a meeting to remember Allah, the angels surround them and the mercy of Allah covers them, and Allah mentions them among the angels.” (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1335","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whenever people sit in a gathering and mention Allah in it and do not send blessings upon the Prophet, that gathering will be a source of regret and regret for them on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"1336","Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever says these words ten times: [There is no God except Allah, and there is no partner for Him, and there is no partner for Him."
"1337","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says [Subhaan Allah wa bihamdiha], ‘Glory be to Allah with His praises and His virtues’ a hundred times, his sins are erased, even if they are equal to the foam of the sea.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1338","It was narrated from Hazrat Juwayriyyah bint Harith that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \"Undoubtedly, I have recited four words after you that if compared with your words, which you have recited from the beginning of the day until now, these words will increase in weight from them.\" Khalqiha Warida Nafsah Wazinah Arsha Wa Middad Kalamata] \"I glorify and praise Allah equal to the number of His creatures and equal to the pleasure of His Self and equal to the weight of His Throne and the brightness of His words.\" (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1339","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: [There is no god but Allah. By Allah] \"There is no god but Allah\" Allah is Glorified \"He is the Greatest\" All praises are for Allah and turning away from evil and doing good is not possible without the power of Allah."
"1340","On the authority of Hazrat Samura bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Four words are the most beloved and favored by Allah. There is no harm in saying any of them first.\" Akbaru] \"Glory be to Allah\" All praises are due to Allah \"There is no god but Allah and Allah is the Greatest\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1341","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) addressed me and said: \"O Abdullah bin Qays! Shall I not tell you one of the treasures of heaven? (He is this:) [La-haul wa wa-la-quwa il-ala-b-il-Allah] “It is not possible to turn away from evil and insist on good except with the help of Allah. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in Nasa'i there is this addition: \"There is no refuge from the punishment of Allah except Allah.\""
"1342","Narrated by Hazrat Nu'man bin Bashir, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, prayer is worship.\" There is a hadith: \"There is nothing more honorable and noble in the sight of Allah than supplication.\""
"1343","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The supplication (made) between the Adhan and Iqamah is not rejected.\""
"1344","On the authority of Hazrat Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Surely your Lord is very shy and modest, generous and generous.\" When the servant spreads his hands in front of him, he is ashamed to return them empty."
